    "title": "Task force nabs murder suspect, another charged with assault - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Vivian Nguyen ,\n3 hours ago MEMPHIS, Tenn. — The Memphis Safe Task Force arrested a man wanted for murder and another man for an aggravated assault on Tuesday.\nAt around 9 p.m., task force members took Kamari West, 21, into custody for first-degree murder.\nKamari West_ Mugshot Courtesy of Shelby County Jail According to the U.S. Marshals Service, they saw West at his house and knocked on the door, and announced they were there to arrest him.\nAgents said West attempted to flee, but once he saw officers, he stopped and was taken into custody. He was wanted for the murder of Jaden Echols in March in Hickory Hill.\nShooting in southwest Memphis leaves man dead MPD said that Echols was taken to the hospital after the shooting, where he later died.\nThey said after his arrest, task force officers and agents searched the home and seized four firearms.\nTask force members were securing the house when they found Marion Metcalf, and he had outstanding warrants for aggravated assault, theft of property, and failure to appear. He was taken into custody.\nAs of Wednesday, agents said that the Memphis Safe Task Force has made 2,095 arrests, seized 366 firearms, located 93 missing children, and arrested 138 gang members.\nKamari West is scheduled to appear in court on Thursday. His bond has not been set.\nMarion Metcalf is scheduled to appear in court in April of next year. His bond has not been set.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WREG.com.\n1",
